From 4f7f0ef7ed953b1cc5e5b30f63c526ae7d04fb14 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nicole Muzzin <nicole@muzz.in>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 18:41:52 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] layout: map Range rects through TextOrigins
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Layout kept two mappings from laid-out characters to DOM offsets, one for
Range rects and one for selection and carets. One mapping now serves
Range.getClientRects, caret stops, caretPositionFromPoint and selection
painting, and it maps characters produced by text-transform exactly, so
carets in uppercased ß or ﬁ text land where Chrome puts them.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
